      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "Transferable human L1 records for polar/nucleotide-like molecules are uniformly below 20%: ATP 3.2–14.9% and 'not bioavailable' at 5000 mg, saquinavir 4%, THU 4.1%, gemcitabine ~10%, levovirin ~10%, didanosine 17%, R1479 6–18%, oxybutynin 7%, phlorizin poor/low, and NHC poor.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C07","C20","C09","C13","C08","C18","C03","C15","C02","C12","C10","C11","C01","C05","C16","C06"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records reinforce low F for the same classes: ATP not bioavailable (C20), compound 4p monkey 10% (C23), saquinavir rat 2.0–4.3% (C25), THU monkey <5% (C26, C34), gemcitabine rat 9.86% and low Cmax (C22, C27), didanosine fed 17–19% (C30, C31), and levovirin monkey 18.4% (C21).",
      "card_ids": ["C20","C23","C25","C26","C34","C22","C27","C30","C31","C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The few above-20% values (levovirin rat 29.3%, NHC mouse 36–56%) are rodent data for small ribonucleosides, not for a 1272 Da corrinoid phosphodiester, and do not outweigh the human low-F records or the query's extreme absorption barrier.",
      "card_ids": ["C28","C32","C33"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "New L3 oral exposure records concern small nucleoside/nucleotide analogs (TDF, decitabine+cedazuridine, entecavir, molnupiravir/NHC) and do not measure F for the query; the near-IV decitabine AUC depends on co-administered cedazuridine, and molnupiravir is a prodrug of NHC, so none are transferable to the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself; the decision relies on transfer from structurally related polar/nucleotide-like contexts and physicochemical priors.",
    "No query-specific dose, formulation, species, or human PK data are available; formulation-dependent absorption cannot be fully excluded.",
    "No direct permeability, first-pass, or efflux measurement is available for the query; the extreme physicochemical profile is supportive but not an endpoint measurement.",
    "L3 oral exposure records are for small nucleoside/nucleotide analogs and do not provide query-specific AUC/Cmax or F."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "The query is a 1272 Da, fully ionized corrinoid/nucleotide-like phosphodiester with TPSA 460 Å² and logD -3.35, exceeding the absorption barriers of every low-F reference context. Human L1/L2 records for polar/nucleotide-like molecules are uniformly below 20%, and the new L3 oral exposure records for small nucleoside analogs do not apply to the query. F >= 20% is not supported; predict low."
}

